> Converted from personal notes. Amounts are for one serving. Directions are editorial, not verified source instructions.

== Ingredients ==

Gather the following ingredients: @chicken thighs{7/20%lb}, @gluten-free pita breads{1}, @olive oil{3/5%tbsp}, @lemon juice{3/5%tbsp}, @garlic cloves{4/5} (minced), @dried oregano{2/5%tsp}, @paprika{1/5%tsp}, @salt{1/5%tsp}, @black pepper{1/10%tsp}, @cherry tomatoes{1/5%cup} (halved), @red onion{1/10} (sliced), @cucumber{1/10} (sliced), @plain Greek yogurt{1/5%cup}, @cucumber{1/10} (grated + drained), @garlic cloves{2/5} (minced), @olive oil{1/5%tbsp}, @lemon juice{1/5%tbsp}, @fresh dill{1/5%tbsp}, @salt{1/20%tsp}.

== Preparation ==

Marinate chicken with the first portions of oil, lemon, garlic and seasonings, then cook fully and slice. Combine yogurt, drained grated cucumber, dill and the remaining dressing ingredients. Warm the gluten-free pita and fill with chicken, vegetables and tzatziki.
